[size=5][b]AI disclosure[/b][/size]
I made this mod with a lot of help from AI, and I'd rather be upfront about it:
[list]
[*]The mod's [b]C# code was written by an AI coding assistant[/b] (Grok) under my direction.
[*]All the bundled art (coats, saddles, pads, bridles and styling) was [b]drawn procedurally by Python scripts[/b] in the repo. Those scripts were also written by AI. The coats are recolours of the vanilla horse sprite's shape with its little built-in saddle painted out, and the tack is drawn from templates. No image-generation model was used for any art.
[*]The [b]mod page text[/b] and the [b]page banner, thumbnail and sprite-sheet gallery images[/b] were also produced with AI help. Those images are the mod's own sprites, scaled up and arranged on a drawn background by an AI-written script. They aren't AI-generated pictures. The gallery also includes [b]real in-game screenshots[/b] I took of the wizard and my horse.
[*]I played it in-game on Windows and it went well, but please report anything you find (which coat + which piece, if something looks misaligned).
[/list]
In line with the Nexus Mods rules, this page is tagged [b]AI-Generated Content[/b] and [b]AI Media[/b].
